# _docs/ai/models.env - model roles for THIS project (stamped by bootstrap.sh from
# templates/_shared/models.env). Single source for every script that names a model.
#
# Values are FAMILY ALIASES the Claude Code CLI resolves to the current iteration of that family
# (`opus`, `sonnet`, `haiku`, `fable`): a release of a newer model needs no edit here, and a
# retired ID can never be typed into an agent file by hand. The resolved model ID is recorded in
# every evaluator verdict header (`resolved:`) and in the delegation ledger, so a phase's verdicts
# are auditable to the exact model that judged them even though the alias moved underneath.
# A full model ID (claude-opus-5-5) is still accepted here when a project must pin.
# scripts/compat-check.sh probes the installed CLI for these aliases once per CLI version; the
# session-start hook announces a missing or stale probe.
#
# Format: KEY=value, no quotes, no spaces around '='. Lines starting with # are ignored.

# Fresh-context evaluator (run-evaluator.sh; also rewritten into .claude/agents/evaluator.md).
# The strongest widely-available family; never downgraded.
EVALUATOR_MODEL=opus

# Delegation-routing roles (delegation-routing skill; chosen per call, these are the names).
MODEL_CHEAP=haiku
MODEL_STANDARD=sonnet
MODEL_STRONG=opus
MODEL_TOP=fable
